# Forex AI System — Trivy vulnerability exceptions (2026-09-11)
#
# Policy: CI (docker-build.yml) scans the exact locally-built production images
# with `trivy image --exit-code 1 --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed`.
# Each entry below is a DOCUMENTED EXCEPTION (justification in audit F-02–F-05
# and docs/phase10-ci-security.md §9). Every line requires a documented entry in
# docs/dependency-security-audit.md. Do not add entries silently — extend only
# with a tracked justification and a removal condition.
#
# To remove an entry: confirm the underlying fix has shipped (base image rebuild,
# upstream patch, or module removal) and that the new scan produces 0 findings for
# that ID.

# --- F-04: RESOLVED (2026-09-11, OpenSSL 3.5.8-r0) ---
# CVE-2026-14456 REMOVED — cleared by targeted OpenSSL package upgrade
# (libcrypto3/libssl3/openssl 3.5.7-r0 → 3.5.8-r0) in the frontend prod stage
# (frontend/Dockerfile). See docs/phase10-base-image-security.md §7.

# --- F-05: npm CLI vendored deps in base image (not app dependencies) ---
# brace-expansion/ip-address/tar live in /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/ (npm
# v11.19.0 shipped inside node:24-alpine). Not in /app; runtime `node server.js`
# never executes npm. No app-level fix — cleared only by upstream node:24-alpine
# npm refresh or removing npm from the image (docs/phase10-remaining-dependency-findings.md §1).
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-73566

# --- F-02: PostCSS (build-time CSS emission only, not shipped to the browser) ---
# postcss@8.4.31 is transitive via next@15.5.25; CSS emission is ephemeral at
# build time. Cleared by upstream patch or next bump.
CVE-2026-45623
CVE-2026-73646

